{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A hundred cubits and its twenty pillars.</b> Each space between them, together with its pillar, was five cubits. However, the twenty pillars of the north and the twenty of the south did not begin directly opposite each other in a straight line; rather, the beginning of one side extended beyond the beginning of the opposite side by the measure of one space, and the pillars of the east and west sides began set back from the extended side by the measure of one space." "<b>And their bands.</b> Rings encircling each pillar at its middle, for beauty."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:23.222079886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}